cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "model-identity-data: names language models choose for themselves (exploratory release)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cyber-audit-lab/model-identity-data"
authors:
  - name: "cyber-audit-lab"
abstract: >-
  Aggregate results of an exploratory study of the names that 39 language models from five families choose when
  asked to name themselves, with matched control prompts, prompt-variation sets and follow-up explanations
  (367,448 answers). Includes a findings report, aggregate tables, figures, prompts and a paper. No full answers or
  per-answer records. Exploratory: no pre-registration was frozen before collection.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - self-naming
  - model identity
  - output diversity
  - mode collapse
  - post-training
